  "title": "Qing dynasty",
  "summary": "The Qing dynasty (1644–1912) was the last imperial dynasty in China. Its Manchu rulers governed from Beijing over one of the largest empires in world history, covering much of East and Central Asia and a multi-ethnic population. Building on the economic developments of the late Ming, it brought prosperity, and also complacency and a dramatic increase in population.",
